# =====================================================================
# Generated / regenerable data -- not source, don't commit.
# The two "!" exceptions below are deliberate; see the notes on each.
# =====================================================================

# Fetched fresh by .github/workflows/etl.yml on every run (rentstab,
# rentstab_v2, HPD violations), so there's no reason to carry them in
# git -- they're large and go stale.
data/raw/*.csv
data/raw/*.json

# The real DHCR building-file PDF and other large manual downloads.
data/raw/*.pdf

# sqlite store -- rebuilt from scratch by the ETL scripts every run.
data/interim/*.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
data/interim/*.csv
# EXCEPTION: parsed from the manually-downloaded DHCR PDF by
# etl/parse_dhcr_pdf.py. The Actions workflow does NOT fetch that PDF and
# does NOT run the parser, so if this file isn't in the repo,
# build_registry.py's load_dhcr_current() logs a warning, returns an
# empty frame, and the workflow commits a registry with on_dhcr_list=0
# on every row -- i.e. it silently throws away the ~16.9k-building DHCR
# signal that is the whole point of the tool. Committed on purpose.
# (A negation after a matching wildcard works because the parent
# directories themselves are not excluded -- git can't re-include a file
# under an excluded directory.)
!data/interim/dhcr_brooklyn_parsed.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
data/processed/*.csv
# EXCEPTION: etl.yml's "Commit updated registry" step runs
# `git add data/processed/registry.csv`. git add on an IGNORED path exits
# 1, and GitHub Actions runs `run:` blocks under `bash -e` -- so with this
# file ignored, that step fails, the weekly workflow fails, and since a
# scheduled workflow on a repo with no commits for 60 days is
# auto-disabled by GitHub, the whole thing quietly switches itself off.
# This is also the file a future GitHub Pages dashboard would read.
#
# NOTE: this is a ~19.5k-row file committed weekly. Git deltas text well
# and most rows won't change, but if the repo gets heavy later, the
# alternative is to keep it ignored and switch etl.yml to `git add -f`.
!data/processed/registry.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Listing data stays OUT of this public repo. matched_listings.csv and
# streeteasy-matches.json contain real addresses, prices and URLs of
# apartments being tracked -- already covered by the wildcards above, but
# spelled out here so a future "!" exception doesn't sweep them in by
# accident. Do not un-ignore these.
data/processed/matched_listings.csv
data/streeteasy-matches.json
**/streeteasy-matches.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# geo/ outputs -- all regenerated on demand.
# parks.geojson: written by geo/load_parks.py (live fetch or placeholder).
# parks_raw.json: the raw Socrata dump from the manual curl step.
# build_geo_output.json: geo/build_geo.py's run output.
# NOTE: geo/park_anchors.json is deliberately NOT ignored -- it's small,
# generated from checked-in source by geo/export_park_anchors.py, and the
# WP5 scheduled task depends on it being pushed to the Claude project.
geo/parks.geojson
geo/parks_raw.json
geo/build_geo_output.json

# =====================================================================
# Secrets -- never commit.
# =====================================================================
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json

# =====================================================================
# Python / editor / OS noise
# =====================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
